What Should the System Improve?

The objective is to improve the quality and trustworthiness of the fitting recommendation, not simply collect more data.

1. Better Head Selection

Determine:

Forgiveness requirement
Launch assistance requirement
Typical miss tendency (slice, hook, push, pull)

Outcome: More appropriate iron/head category selection.

2. Better Shaft Selection

Determine:

Estimated clubhead speed
Swing tempo
Transition aggressiveness
Release timing (if feasible)

Outcome: More accurate shaft flex, weight, and profile recommendation.

3. Better Lie & Length Recommendation

Refine:

Height
Wrist-to-floor
Setup posture

Outcome: Improved lie angle and club length recommendations.

4. Confidence & Transparency

For every recommendation provide:

Confidence score
Evidence used
Alternative viable options

Outcome: Increased user trust.

5. Eliminate Poor Fits

Instead of finding one "perfect" club:

Exclude clearly unsuitable heads
Exclude unsuitable shaft categories
Explain why

Outcome: Narrow the solution space to a set of valid options rather than a single unexplained recommendation.

Required Outputs

The fitting system should produce:

Category	Output
Player Profile	Forgiveness need, launch need, miss tendency
Swing Profile	Speed, tempo, transition, release
Physical Profile	Height, wrist-to-floor, hand size, posture
Recommendation Quality	Confidence, alternatives, eliminated options, reasoning
Key Requirement

The system should help golfers understand why a recommendation was made and why other options were excluded, not just recommend a club.